    "result_text": "Done. There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and the full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asked for an immutable structured `OWNER_CREATED` event via the `AUDIT` logger \u2014 `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event}` \u2014 with a monotonically increasing `seq`, carrying the owner's *current primary identifier* so it can later swap from `customerCode` to `memberId`.\n\nI made all changes in a **single file**, `OwnerAuditPolicy.java`, keeping structural impact minimal:\n\n- Added a `static final AtomicLong SEQ` counter (monotonic across creates).\n- Added a tiny `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` helper that returns `getCustomerCode()` today \u2014 the single point to change when the code unifies into `memberId`, so the event automatically carries the new identifier later.\n- Added a small, self-contained `auditCreatedEvent(Owner)` method (CC 1) that emits the JSON event.\n- Added exactly one line to `auditCreate` to invoke it.\n\nThe existing plain audit line is untouched, and I avoided editing the large controller's `addOwner` method (high surrounding complexity) entirely \u2014 the event rides on the already-wired `auditCreate` call site.\n\nVerified output:\n```\nAUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
